{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486069-understanding-the-nwod-current-state-of-mythos-vampires-mummies-rome-egypt-strix","id":486069,"title":"Understanding the nWoD current state of mythos (Vampires, Mummies, Rome, Egypt, Strix ...)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-20T00:24:59-07:00","id":486069,"title":"Understanding the nWoD current state of mythos (Vampires, Mummies, Rome, Egypt, Strix ...)","content":"<b>TL;DR : What is the closest equivalent to a unifying mythos/story across game lines, especially in Vampire, Werewolves, Mummies, Hunter and such?</b> Any link you would recommend?<br /> <br /> While reading other threads (such as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32125-obtenebration-and-the-strix\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-and-the-strix</a>, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/103254-putting-together-the-pieces-sethite-mekhet-the-khaibit-and-the-ascending-ones\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ascending-ones</a>), I had the vertiginous impression of not understanding anything about the implied storylines of nWoD, including Requiem's.<br /> <br /> I thought I &quot;got&quot; it when I read the Vampire translation guide, that the scheming of the powerful, their conspiracies of silence, webs of lies, added to the <i>Fog of Eternity</i>, and even (in our own world) very real historical distance &quot;make proving or disproving any given creation story impossible&quot;, that &quot;the system treats none of them as more or less valid than any other&quot;, &quot;many stories exist, but less evidence points to one being true&quot;. And I already know that I can dismiss what I don't want and create my own, it's all fine and dandy, even to my modernist objectivity-hungry brain (post-structuralist French Theory has to be a personal Bane dealing aggravated damage or causing me derangements...).<br /> <br /> Of course, Vampire the Masquerade's unifying meta-plot is easier for me to get a grasp / intuitive understanding of...<br /> <br /> But despite being different from Masquerade, signs point out to a certain linked, semi-unifying meta-plot, at least for the world's past even in Requiem and the other nWoD game lines. While I can easily keep or dismiss whatever I want, cobbling cross-over games mixing Vampires with Egyptian names, a roman &quot;Fall of the Camarilla&quot;, Mummies, Khaibit vampire bloodlines, etc. Dracula, etc. ...it basically begs the question of, basically,<b> what is THE &quot;story so far&quot;</b>.<br /> <br /> There is necessarily a story, because there is stuff you can't deny exists. Mekhet being a word requires an Egyptian origin of some sort, or at least an interaction. The Ordo Dracul requires a Dracula or some sort. What about the Strix? The Invictus implies a Camarilla and a relation to Roman history... and Egypt, which at some point was part of the Empire, which is not very far from Palestine where Longinus speared Jesus on the cross... etc.<br /> <br /> Is there a good timeline of events, summary, or global explanation of the various events? (I am asking because I actually want to know, not because I feel forced to know it.)<br /> <br /> I know for a fact, especially as a player, that &quot;not knowing&quot; is a pleasure in and of itself, &quot;Mystery Box&quot; and all. But the fun in Mystery is being confident that behind all the false leads, there IS <i>actually </i>an explanation, even (and especially) if it's a totally unexpected kind of explanation! As a prospective GM this summer, my players are going to expect some degree of truth to be found behind the many layers of falsehoods and red herrings. (Or else, what's the point of searching ?) I want to be able to decide what truth there will be, after having had a good look at what nWoD has in store.<br /> <br /> Basically, I know I can make my own stories or my own rules, I fully intend to be creative, but if someone uses weird egyptian words, mentions Rome or some historical time, they better have some idea of what was going on then so I can know if I want to use it or not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5602,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","user":"BarbeChenue","date":". 04-20-2015, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T01:30:44-07:00","id":486115,"title":"","content":"I'm afraid, that there is no thing as a storyline. There are a lot of myths, but they don't have to be true.<br /> <br /> Yes, Mekhet in General have a Egyptian origin, but what is with the Scandinavian Bloodline, who claims origin from a entire different Clan? It isn't sure, that the vampires of the different Clans share a common origin, but it is'n sure as well, that the Vampires of the same Clan share the same origin. Every clan has different originstories, they all could be true, they all don't have to.<br /> <br /> The nWoD is much more like our world, many people claim many things. Not everyone is trustworthy and not everyone is a liar.<br /> <br /> The things we know are not much more than that:<br /> <br /> Vampires exist and they do pretty much as long as mankind. In Rome one now lost Clan started to create a vampire society known as Camarilla. This Clan had betrayed the Strix, who are, or who are not the creators of all Vampires. The Strix believe that and hunt vampires for that, but it don't have be true.<br /> <br /> After the fall of the Camarilla something happens, which no one remembers. After that the Julii, the founder of the Camarilla disappeared and the Ventrue appear. They may, or may not be related to the lost Julii.<br /> <br /> Every covenant has his own story, they are roughly believable but propaganda as well.<br /> <br /> In the last decades the Strix, who where rather quiet in the meantime came back to punish the Vampires.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> You could discover the \u201ctruth\u201d behind a thing every time. And it might seem like the Truth for the character, but in fact it is just another layer of the truth and maybe a false evidence.<br /> <br /> You do not have to understand the History of the nWoD. You just have to keep it vague. There are only personal trueths, not general ones. Concentrate on the characters, not on the metaplot which do not exist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T03:46:22-07:00","id":486193,"title":"","content":"Lemme see what I can come up with:<br /> <br /> <b>Distant Past</b> - the first vampires appear.<br /> <br /> The first vampires seem to have been the result of a sort of symbiosis between early humans and <i>something else</i>. There is no singular moment of creation; the clan probably arose separately in different places and times. The Mekhet clanbook seems to suggest that that clan is descended from some kind of primordial, predatory being that encountered humans somewhere in central Africa early in the history of our species. Some or all of the clans may have been created by the Strix, either deliberately or by accident; the Strix certainly like to claim as much.<br /> <br /> <b>c. 1835 - 1739 BCE</b> - the rise of En Isiratuu<br /> <br /> A powerful Daeva known as Isiratuu becomes En (&quot;lord&quot; or &quot;god&quot;) of Babylon's Kindred with the aid of a mysterious &quot;Alu&quot; or &quot;Dark Stranger.&quot; Through the strange powers granted to him by the Alu, he will rule for around 12,000 years and extend his influence throughout the Near East.<br /> <br /> <b>1352 - 1280 BCE </b>- The reign of Akhenaten.<br /> <br /> By this time, vampires of all 5 of the major clans were present in Egypt (though the Ventrue were a relatively minor group), and had organized themselves into bloodlines covenants connected with the temples of the major Egyptian gods. Akhenaten's attempts to break the power of Egypt's traditional temples and replace them with his own brand of monotheism causes a lot of trouble for these early vampire organizations.<br /> <br /> <b>1279 BCE</b> - The rise of Ramesses the Great<br /> <br /> The leader of the Bak-Ra, Mekhet worshipers of the Egyptian sun god, makes Ramesses II into a ghoul, facilitating his long reign as Pharaoh, which brought great prosperity to Egypt. Around this same time, the Bak-Ra use the chaos following the reign of Akhenaten to consolidate the various vampiric temple factions into a &quot;Great Covenant&quot; under their leadership. This power structure remained in place, largely unchanged, until some time after the Roman conquest of Egypt.<br /> <br /> <b>12th Century BCE</b> - The Aenead<br /> <br /> According to traditional histories of the Ventrue clan, Aeneas carries the ancestors of the Ventrue from the ruins of Troy to their new home in Latium, the region that will one day give rise to the city of Rome. Some Ventrue possibly remain in Anatolia.<br /> <br /> <b>c. 758 - 738 BCE</b> - The founding of Rome<br /> <br /> Rome is founded by Romulus, who slays his brother Remus for obstructing his work. The Strix appear to Remus as he dies, and transform him into a vampire. Later generations of kindred in Rome will claim that he was the first vampire to call the city home, and his descendants will come to rule over the vampires of the Roman Empire.<br /> <br /> <b>750 BCE</b> - The Rape of the Sabine Women<br /> <br /> The men of Rome abduct women from the neighboring Sabine tribe to be their wives. Following this event, Remus embraces his first Childe, Aulus Julius, who would go on to become the patriarch of the Julii clan. Romulus sets him to work digging a network of tunnels under Rome in which their descendants will live. The Nosferatu of Rome claim that five of their clan were already in the area at the time, and aided Romulus in building his Necropolis.<br /> <br /> <b>635 - 539 BCE</b> - the Neo-Babylonian Empire<br /> <br /> By this time, members of all five major clans are present in Mesopotamia. At some point during this period, En Isiratuu is destroyed through the machinations of the equally ancient Mekhet sorceress, Nanshi Iltani, who unleashes seven destructive spirits known as the Edimmu (who bear some resemblance to the Strix) upon the kindred of the Babylonian Empire. The Edimmu proceed to tear the existing kindred power structures of the Near East apart, and by the time the kindred have exterminated them, they have come together into a single covenant known as the United in order to ensure their mutual survival.<br /> <br /> <b>c. 600 BCE</b> - The disappearance of Remus<br /> <br /> Remus disappears from the Roman Necropolis around this time; his fate is unknown. Aulus Julius becomes ruler of the kindred in Rome.<br /> <br /> <b>509 BCE</b> - The Fall of the Unnamed Clan<br /> <br /> The Strix appear to Aulus Julius about 100 years after the disappearance of Remus to demand a tithe of mortal family members from the kindred of Rome. Aulus and the Julii find this demand too much to bear, but another, unnamed clan opposes them, insisting that Remus made a compact with the Strix, and that any demand made by the owls must be met. Aulus condemns the unnamed clan, and the other vampires of the city turned on them. The whole of the clan is exterminated on the same night that Tarquin the Proud, the last king of Rome, is overthrown in a popular uprising.<br /> <br /> Some time afterward, Aulus Julius declares that the vampires of Rome should have a senate of their own, and establishes the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <b>c. 450 - 400 BCE</b> - Aulus Julius enters Torpor<br /> <br /> Some time during this period Aulus Julius voluntarily falls into Torpor. As far as history records, he never re-awakens.<br /> <br /> <b>c. 200 BCE</b> - The Daeva Arrive in Rome<br /> <br /> Following the second Punic War, Daeva from north Africa probably start taking an interest in Rome and her kindred.<br /> <br /> <b>52 BCE</b> - The Gangrel Arrive in Rome<br /> <br /> A group of Gallic Gangrel follow Julius Caesar's army, and eventually come to the city of Rome itself.<br /> <br /> <b>c. 46 BCE</b> - The Mekhet Arrive in Rome<br /> <br /> Cleopatra visits Rome with a luxurious entourage, charming the citizens and sparking a period of fascination with Egypt in the city. Mekhet from Egypt first rise to prominence in Rome during this period, though there may already have been some of the clan in the city.<br /> <br /> <b>c. 30 CE</b> - Crucifixion of Jesus<br /> <br /> Jesus Christ is crucified in Rome. According to the <i>Testament of Longinus</i>, the centurion Longinus is cursed by God with vampirism after driving a spear into the side of Christ and tasting his blood.<br /> <br /> <b>c. 62 CE</b> - The Vision of Vahishtael<br /> <br /> According to the <i>Testament</i>, Longinus is visited by the angel Vahishtael, who reveals to him his holy purpose.<br /> <br /> <b>64 CE</b> - The Great Fire of Rome<br /> <br /> Four-fifths of the kindred in Rome die during the great fire and in the chaos of it's aftermath. The Camarilla is forced to more-or-less rebuild itself from the ground up.<br /> <br /> <b>72 CE</b> - The Siege of Masada<br /> <br /> The Monachus, the first of Longinus' disciples, is supposedly present at the end of the Siege of Masada with his four childer, where he embraces the fifth, Daniel. This, however, does not seem to agree with the chronology presented earlier in the text. Regardless, Longinus presumably embraced (or recruited, since some argue that Longinus never embraced a childe) the Monachus some time before this point, and by this time has already disappeared.<br /> <br /> <b>262 CE</b> - Thascius Hostilinus Arrives in Rome<br /> <br /> Thascius Hostilinus, a Numidian vampire whom the <i>Testament</i> mentions as being one of the vampires converted by Daniel, childe of the Monachus, in Egypt, arrives in Rome to preach to the Roman kindred, according to the <i>Testimony of the Plague Angel</i>. Hostilinus is possibly the founder of the Morbus bloodline, and is perhaps the most prominent leader of the Lancea et Sanctum in Rome prior to the fall of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <b>286 CE</b> - The Martyrdom of the Theban Legion<br /> <br /> The legendary Theban Legion, a Roman Legion originally station in Thebes, Egypt that had converted en-masse to Christianity, is executed on a battlefield in Gaul for refusing to sacrifice to the gods of Rome. Daniel has been with them since they were in Thebes, where he learned Theban Sorcery with the help of the angel Amoniel. Daniel turns on the remaining Roman soldiers, killing many before being consumed in a pillar of divine fire. Other kindred hiding among the army convert on the spot. <br /> <br /> Note that modern (mortal) historians doubt that the legend of the Theban Legion has any basis in fact.<br /> <br /> Some time after these events, the Monachus' two remaining disciples were martyred, one in Thebes (by a &quot;worshiper of Seth&quot;) and one in the Italian Alps. The Monachus subsequently went on to found the Black Abbey somewhere north of the Alps, but the Abbey itself is a topic of myth and speculation, and its history is largely unknown.<br /> <br /> <b>410 AD</b> - The Fall of the Camarilla<br /> <br /> During the sack of Rome by the army of Alaric I, the Strix emerge in great numbers to prey upon the kindred of Rome, apparently as revenge for the slaughter of the unnamed clan and the violation of the compact they had made with Remus. Within a relatively short period the majority of Rome's vampires have been destroyed, the Julii clan has been apparently entirely exterminated, and the Camarilla is no more. The Lancea et Sanctum steps in to fill the power vacuum.<br /> <br /> <b>1142 AD</b> - The Founding of the Invictus<br /> <br /> Aelfgifu, a Ventrue Elder from the Rhine valley, persuades a group of secular princes from across the Holy Roman Empire to assemble in Rome, in the underground council chamber once used by the Camarilla, to establish a new ruling body for the vampires of Europe. Although the influence of this new alliance initially only extended to a handful of domains in the HRE, the philosophies and principals it established quickly spread, eventually growing into the modern Invictus.<br /> <br /> <b>1204 AD</b> - The Sack of Constantinople<br /> <br /> The crusader army of Boniface I, Marquess of Montferrat, captures and sacks Constantinople during the fourth crusade. A group of western European vampires affiliated with the nascent Invictus swoops in to seize power, breaking the strength of the <i>Adamantes Athanatoi</i>, an eastern offshoot of the Camarilla that had ruled over the vampires of the Byzantine Empire. Although they cease to exist as a governing body, the survivors of the <i>Adamantes Athanatoi</i> will exert a great deal of influence on the subsequent development of the Invictus.<br /> <br /> <b>c. 1476</b> - Dracula becomes a Vampire<br /> <br /> According to the <i>Rites of the Dragon</i>, Vlad III of Wallachia rises as a vampire with no sire, having been cursed by God after falling in battle with the Turks.<br /> <br /> <b>Late 15th - Late 16th Centuries</b> - The Inquisition<br /> <br /> The early modern &quot;Inquisition&quot;, more properly a witch-hunting craze that swept over Europe without any real central organization or planning, had a surprisingly profound effect on the vampires of the day, effectively demolished the web of alliances that had defined the European Invictus during the middle ages, as many elders met their final deaths and those who remained were forced to be subtler in their machinations. This marked the end of any serious attempt at a centralized vampire &quot;government&quot; in the west.<br /> <br /> <b>Early 17th Century</b> - Birth of the Ordo Dracul<br /> <br /> By this point the <i>Rites of the Dragon</i> are in fairly wide circulation, and just as occultism has come into vogue with the mortal nobility of the day, the Ordo Dracul finds many recruits, who establish the structure and titles used by the covenant to this day.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> There's more, but I just noticed what time it was, and I need to get some sleep. Hope this helps, though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 04-20-2015, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T05:29:46-07:00","id":486261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486069-understanding-the-nwod-current-state-of-mythos-vampires-mummies-rome-egypt-strix#post486069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>TL;DR : What is the closest equivalent to a unifying mythos/story across game lines, especially in Vampire, Werewolves, Mummies, Hunter and such?</b> Any link you would recommend?<br /> <br /> There is necessarily a story, because there is stuff you can't deny exists. Mekhet being a word requires an Egyptian origin of some sort, or at least an interaction. T<u>he Ordo Dracul requires a Dracula or some sort</u>. What about the Strix? The Invictus implies a Camarilla and a relation to Roman history... and Egypt, which at some point was part of the Empire, which is not very far from <u>Palestine where Longinus speared Jesus on the cross... etc</u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it?<br /> I been watching some lectures by Dr. Richard Carrier and Robert M Price on the Historicity of Christ, and I been thinking maybe there is no Dracula or Loginus.<br /> Claiming a famous founder has always help movements. Look at how both parties claim Jefferson and Hamilton.<br /> <br /> Mekhet I'll give you. There is an Egyption line but who is to say there isn't another independent line of shadowy occult vampires who had their grave desecrated from another part of the world. They are just known as Mekhet today.<br /> <br /> Ven and Julii, that weird first edition reference about the Nosferatu being a relatively new clan but there was an ancient clan like them?<br /> And now spontaneous embracing has escaped the Nos clan book and Requiem for Rome into the main books. It is clear even if a clan is wiped out It or something like it will arise again when conditions are right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T07:07:51-07:00","id":486308,"title":"","content":"To be honest, a lot of what was 'known' in 1.0 (like, we know certain political trends and certain bloodlines from periods) may or may not exist now. I mean, according to the Ordo Dracul book, there were vampires who claim to have been sired by Dracula active as late as the late 19th century. Nowadays, who knows? (until Secrets of the Covenants comes out)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T07:09:18-07:00","id":486309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486069-understanding-the-nwod-current-state-of-mythos-vampires-mummies-rome-egypt-strix?p=486261#post486261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it?<br /> I been watching some lectures by Dr. Richard Carrier and Robert M Price on the Historicity of Christ, and I been thinking maybe there is no Dracula or Loginus.<br /> Claiming a famous founder has always help movements. Look at how both parties claim Jefferson and Hamilton.<br /> <br /> Mekhet I'll give you. There is an Egyption line but who is to say there isn't another independent line of shadowy occult vampires who had their grave desecrated from another part of the world. They are just known as Mekhet today.<br /> <br /> Ven and Julii, that weird first edition reference about the Nosferatu being a relatively new clan but there was an ancient clan like them?<br /> And now spontaneous embracing has escaped the Nos clan book and Requiem for Rome into the main books. It is clear even if a clan is wiped out It or something like it will arise again when conditions are right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what BarbeChenue would like, is to know what the truth might be behind the world we're playing in. A lot of people used to buy RPGs (including VtM) just for the fiction and setting, never running or playing in a single chronicle themselves.<br /> <br /> That said, 2e seems to me like the end of the era of experimentation for nWoD and the maturity of a setting open-ended enough to allow STs easr of customization, while also providing us with a more concrete setting overall (no more sanbox).<br /> <br /> The teased Theban Sorcery rituals do include, after all, a certain epiklesis to Belial, which demonstrates how much 2e might have changed things.<br /> <br /> Let's see how this goes. Truly interesting stuff going on...<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, the scientific method of theory formulation and reliability should not, in the WoD, be what it is in real life. While in WoD many Kindred will claim these lectures disprove Longinus or Dracula, the truth should at least be more confusing and metaphysical than the prevalent mythos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 04-20-2015, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T07:46:43-07:00","id":486359,"title":"","content":"I'm totally amazed by that timeline! This is the kind of stuff I'd like to see, as a Storyteller.<br /> <br /> While I relish the freedom to refuse a given &quot;origin story&quot; or explanation, and thus not feel constrained in my imagination, this doesn't preclude there <i>being</i> a default story in the book in the first place from which I could depart or base myself. The problem with multiple seperated / unrelated origin stories with no overarching / encompassing logic is that you might end up in a messy kitchen sink experience if you mix too many things together. It's much easier to justify <i>many </i>supernaturals if you make them related to a common (set of) metaphysic(s) that if you have to start anew each time.<br /> <br /> To be clear, if each bloodline, each clan, each covenant, each werewolf tribe or lodge, each hunter conspiracy or compact, the mummy book, etc. if each of them have a different set of origin stories that are neither true or false, imagine the number of variables you have to take into account if you want to include any of them...<br /> <br /> Which is not to say I would like to be handed a unified setting, such as Star Wars (which now has One Canon To Rule Them All). I think there is a margin between the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T08:01:18-07:00","id":486390,"title":"","content":"What you're supposed to do is ignore all the various origin stories unless it actually comes up as a plot point. It ultimately <i>doesn't matter</i> what the real origins of vampires or werewolves were. What's important is what they're doing <i>now. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T08:08:14-07:00","id":486410,"title":"","content":"We all know our players, mine explicitly *will* want to find out.<br /> I've played with groups that couldn't even be bothered to investigate a very obvious plot <i>against them</i>, with abundant clues and all...<br /> And I have seen other groups that will try to pierce the veneer of reality in each and every world they play in, trying to get a grasp of the hidden metaphysics of it, up to filling binders of notes.<br /> <br /> The group I'll GM this summer is of the second sort, so I don't have much of a choice. (And I enjoy this too, worry not!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T08:21:06-07:00","id":486413,"title":"","content":"Oh, I do the same. My Grand Unified Theory of the WoD generally drags in Exalted for the lulz though, so it's not something I'd make explicit in-play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T09:27:56-07:00","id":486465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486069-understanding-the-nwod-current-state-of-mythos-vampires-mummies-rome-egypt-strix?p=486359#post486359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, if each bloodline, each clan, each covenant, each werewolf tribe or lodge, each hunter conspiracy or compact, the mummy book, etc. if each of them have a different set of origin stories that are neither true or false, imagine the number of variables you have to take into account if you want to include any of them...</div> </div> </div> </div>As a point of clarity, the whole &quot;one creature type, many origins&quot; is specifically a vampire thing, and more than that, it's just the Clans. Each Clan has at least one origin story, some, all, or none of which may be true due to all available narrators being extremely unreliable. But bloodlines can all be traced back to a single progenitor as they're literally direct lines of embrace. The Covenants were also founded at specific points in history (although the 5 covenants in the core book are not the only ones, many others have come and gone, or exist in other parts of the world.)<br /> <br /> Werewolves have a single origin. They are all distant descendants of Luna and <i>Urfarah</i>, or so their legends say - unlike vampires, werewolves are not immortal, and since their history is primarily oral tradition, no one knows for sure. There are occasionally spontaneous Wolf-Blooded, but they can be put down to Luna's whimsy. Auspices are just the moon phase they first change under, and Tribes and Lodges are organizations founded at a specific point in history.<br /> <br /> Hunter Compacts and Conspiracies, same deal. Specific organization, specific founding. I don't know anything about Mummy, but I assume origins are pretty specific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T09:33:19-07:00","id":486472,"title":"","content":"Mummy would be the most concrete one of all if the protags could remember it, because they were all <i>there. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T09:39:43-07:00","id":486475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486069-understanding-the-nwod-current-state-of-mythos-vampires-mummies-rome-egypt-strix?p=486465#post486465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;snip&gt;<br /> Hunter Compacts and Conspiracies, same deal. Specific organization, specific founding. I don't know anything about Mummy, but I assume origins are pretty specific.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Mummy guy, I can confirm that it's pretty explicit about the origins of its protagonists: all Mummies were created by the sorcerer-priests of the Nameless Empire during the Rite of Return 6000 years ago. They were selected from the ranks of middle-class laborers, guildsmen, crafters, priests, and lawyers. The guilds were formed by the sorcerer-kings to be specialized labor, naturally.<br /> <br /> There <i>are</i> lots of questions that arise in the setting, but few of them are related to history or origins. They're more like, &quot;What was I doing between 456 and 500 CE, and why does it seem to have something to do with the ancient ghosts of these Roman Legionnaires and a seedy corporate cult trying to steal my relics?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T09:46:45-07:00","id":486478,"title":"","content":"While Mummies are probably clear on when things happened, they weren't the ones who performed the Rite of Return, their knowledge of the whys and wherefores would be limited even with perfect recall.<br /> <br /> Back to BarbeChenue, if you're interested in an absolute truth about things, you're going to have to make it yourself. You can use one of the many possible origins or make one up yourself. No matter how interested your players or their characters are in the history of the world, they won't find the 'right' answer until you decide which one you want to be right in the first place. Though if they're reading the books for the fluff they've probably already made their minds up.<br /> <br /> The only real consistent thing throughout all the gamelines is that their histories tend to be entwined with the history of western civilization, from the fertile crescent and onward, sort of glossing over eastern Asia and the majority of Africa, except for a few stand out bloodlines. The more recent an event, the better the records of it, such as the founding of the Dragolescu bloodline, the farther back in history, the more unclear it is. The only standout might be werewolves, who might have evolved parallel to humanity in the Border Marches.<br /> <br /> Also, since we have the Rome books, and the Dark Eras stuff is out, you can see what things were like at certain times. Neolithic Mage and Werewolf is likely to shine some light on some of their origins, and will have a sidebar saying what everyone else is up to.<br /> <br /> There's a simple sentence in the Mekhet clan book that sort of puts it all in perspective, as one of Francis' past lives or past sires is feeding blood to a high priest and using what I think is dominate to influence him. Once Dominate popped up, you can't trust anything. The Ventrue in their own clanbook assure you they're descended from gods and kings, to the point that it extends to the Gangrel book, where a Ventrue is reaffirming this to Alice. But it really seems like they are just lying about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-20-2015, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T10:55:00-07:00","id":486507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486069-understanding-the-nwod-current-state-of-mythos-vampires-mummies-rome-egypt-strix?p=486413#post486413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I do the same. My Grand Unified Theory of the WoD generally drags in Exalted for the lulz though, so it's not something I'd make explicit in-play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny that you would mention that - once a friend made an &quot;Exalted Modern&quot; game, with some hints here and there that Creation became the nWoD that he never really explored, so i ended up writing some stuff connecting vampiric origins to a mix of necromantic curses that kept working even though some of its casters were long gone and virtue/grace-like developments among the &quot;masterless&quot; undead so generated, among other fun stuff, like Wolfman &amp; Kid (Angel-inspired supernatural corp/firm lead by 3 lines of descendants of Maha-Su-Chi) and others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-20-2015, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T11:40:12-07:00","id":486573,"title":"","content":"I can't help but ponder how Father Wolf being a Lunar <i>would</i> explain a few things, like how werewolves ended up half-human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T13:37:12-07:00","id":486699,"title":"","content":"It might be prudent to move this to the general boards so folks that frequent the other subforums might pitch in!<br /> <br /> I believe there's a sidebar in one of the Idigam's writeups, or maybe at the start of it? That discusses a theory as to how Werewolves got the human part, though I can't recall it off the top of my head and don't have access to my pdf at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T13:44:31-07:00","id":486704,"title":"","content":"In the 2Ed Werewolf it is mentioned, that even not all Werewolfs believe the Story of Father/Mother Wolf and Father/Mother Moon. It is mentioned as the most common, but there are still Werewolfs who believe a variant or totally reject the Story as myths or metaphor.<br /> <br /> The thing with the truth is, that there is no thing like that. There are just viewpoints. When I am leading VtM (Yes, the Game with the huge Metaplot) I constantly let my players figure out \u201cthe truth\u201d. After that I let them play with the knowledge of it. They make decisions, act in the way they think is the right one and fight against people who are enemies of the truth. After that, I pull away the curtain and reveal a more \u201ctrue\u201d truth and they have to realize, everything they had done with the best intentions was wrong, stupid or even meaningless. And so on and on and on... They love it, and I am too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T14:15:23-07:00","id":486719,"title":"","content":"The second edition brings in the possibility that becoming a vampire is a simply possible part of the human condition, just as a human can become a Mage. Maybe several &quot;Daeva-like&quot; beings arose over the centuries, dancing their way into the condition with an extreme lust for the (shallow?) aspects of life powerful enough to overcome death. With enough interchanging of blood any line of descent that is &quot;Daeva-like&quot; simply becomes &quot;Daeva&quot;. In other words the five major clans are common themes, even an independent lineage typically converges around one over time.<br /> <br /> Doesn't have to be this way of course, but I prefer it. It makes the vampire &quot;tree of life&quot; a tangled mess, five big branches resulting from many smaller ones weaving together, branching off and folding back in again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T14:29:02-07:00","id":486727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486069-understanding-the-nwod-current-state-of-mythos-vampires-mummies-rome-egypt-strix?p=486699#post486699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be prudent to move this to the general boards so folks that frequent the other subforums might pitch in!<br /> <br /> I believe there's a sidebar in one of the Idigam's writeups, or maybe at the start of it? That discusses a theory as to how Werewolves got the human part, though I can't recall it off the top of my head and don't have access to my pdf at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lodge of Quicksilver Children think they have an answer, but it is pretty apocryphal. Basically, they believe werewolves were not actually the children of Luna and Wolf, but that the two of them have birth to an Idigam, which then made some kind of pact with a human sorcerer, and the Uratha are a result of that arrangement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T15:21:20-07:00","id":486760,"title":"","content":"I have a few theories regarding some of the big &quot;mysteries&quot; of Vampire, though whether they're &quot;true&quot; or not is probably mostly immaterial in any modern Chronicle I'd run.<br /> <br /> *Remus was never a vampire, and probably never existed. Aulus Julius made him up in order to give his brood of Roman vampires an origin myth that legitimized their rule over the kindred of the city. Also, he probably wasn't as old as he claimed to be. However, it is true that the founder of the Julii (Aulus, in this case) was not embraced in the traditional manner, but rather became a vampire when a Strix merged with his body. The unusual nature of his embrace accounts for the small differences that separated the Julii from the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> <br /> *The &quot;Unnamed Clan&quot; of Rome were the Latin Ventrue, who had been in the region for some time, although they probably weren't brought there by Aeneas. They might have come there following the ancestors of the Etruscans, who are believed to have come from Anatolia. There are a number of possible reasons that they might have aligned themselves with the Strix, but in any case they were exterminated in the area and did not return until after the fall of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Longinus never existed. The vampire who would become known to history as the Monachus was a devout early Christian who received the embrace, and subsequently dreamed up the dogma of the Sanctified in order to justify his unnatural existence. He was probably at least a little bit mad. He penned most of the <i>Testament</i> himself, though other early Sanctified added to it to create its &quot;modern&quot; form, and he cobbled the plot of the text together from bits of existing Christian folklore and his own diseased imagination.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Theban Sorcery doesn't actually have any particular link to the Judeo-Christian cosmology; it's an ancient form of blood magic developed by the Great Covenant of Egyptian vampires, much of which had been lost in the upheavals following the Roman conquest of Egypt. The &quot;angel&quot; Amoniel may have been a member of the Bak-Ra using a devotion to project his consciousness and image out of his body, in order to impress the Monachus and his disciples. His reason for introducing them to Theban sorcery is unknown, but it's likely that he intended to in some way bend the young covenant to his own will. He may have succeeded.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Dracula was one of the kindred, but he was the result of an unintentional embrace by a Turkish vampire and not a unique creature cursed by God. His philosophy was significantly influenced by the beliefs of the Mystikoi bloodline of the Gangrel, who adhered to a strange, Gnostic version of the Sanctified doctrine. He likely encountered members of the bloodline while in the Ottoman empire, early in his unlife.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Most of these are ideas implied, to one degree or another, in the text of various supplements; there's nothing terribly groundbreaking about them. I am rather pleased to have come up with the idea of a Bak-Ra elder trying to hijack the nascent Lancea Sanctum, and that his plots might continue to have consequences in modern nights. I also think it might be interesting for the Monachus to still be out there, somewhere. What he knows could shake the Lancea Sanctum to its core, but his mind is so broken by millennia of lies and self-loathing that he's no longer capable of telling it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 04-20-2015, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T15:39:42-07:00","id":486772,"title":"","content":"Love your ideas. I also had thought about most of them in the past. Except the Bak-Ra one (which I love).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T17:17:38-07:00","id":486876,"title":"","content":"I think CatDoom's answers provide the most grounded reading of the text, and probably the one I'd use. The Bak-Ra one is particularly evident in their writeup, though it also begs the question where <i>they </i>got it from.<br /> <br /> I've never thought to consider the <i>Traditores </i>were Rome's Ventrue, though. That's a real nice idea, I love it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T07:56:19-07:00","id":487266,"title":"","content":"OK, I realize I could elaborate a bit on my initial question:<br /> <br /> I think my issue is trying to come up with believable cross-over scenarios involving supernatural entities, magical metaphysics, and a collective core of occult knowledge across lines. History is part of that &quot;unifying&quot; attempt, but the goal is cross-over compatibility.<br /> <br /> I know there are quite a few paragraphs spread out in different books about the relationships between Werewolves, Vampires, and Mages, plus luckily Hunter, Prometheans, Mummies, Changelings, Sin-eaters, and Demons, etc. But is there a sourcebook or collected body of information that could help put together a coherent whole?<br /> <br /> For example, in the Circle of the Crone seems to have beliefs partially compatible with Werewolves, or at the very least a discussion could be had. Also, all Hunter books, for good reason, <i>do </i>talk about their preferred enemies.<br /> <br /> <b>TL;DR</b> What kind of support for cross-overs should I be looking for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T08:05:06-07:00","id":487292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486069-understanding-the-nwod-current-state-of-mythos-vampires-mummies-rome-egypt-strix#post486069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TL;DR : What is the closest equivalent to a unifying mythos/story across game lines, especially in Vampire, Werewolves, Mummies, Hunter and such? Any link you would recommend?</div> </div> </div> </div> Here it is, the grand unifying mythos of the World of Darkness:<br /> <br /> <b>Once upon a time, there was the dark, and mankind knew not how deep it went or what dwelt there.</b><br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, if the goal is crossover compatibility, then don't worry abut anything. Just explore relationships between them as they go,have fun with it.<br /> <br /> As an aid, remember that the following don't have conceptsof building groups strictly out of their own kind: Werewolf packs don't need all werewolves, pact-bound motleys don't need changelings, ceremony-bound krewes....might not need Sin-Eaters, scorpion cults don't need humans to fill the ranks, and broods thrive off of crossover.<br /> <br /> Beast the Primordial is the closest to openly talking about crossover, and it's not yet, and that aisdes any crossover bits are more or less scattered to the winds and left for discussion(Tome of the Mysteries, Equinox Road and Rites of Spring, kinda sorta Splintered City: Seattle, etc.), but running crossover is easy-look for things in common and things in difference and have fun with them.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I thought this was in the World of Darkness thread, didn't realize it was in Vampire the Requiem. Silly me!<br /> <br /> The same applies. I just needed to acknowledge my snafu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-21-2015, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T08:06:42-07:00","id":487294,"title":"","content":"You might be able to have a Circle of the Crone covey that follows the moon-as-Crone, but there isn't really a default assumption of that sort of crossover. In this particular instance reading about the Circle of the Crone would probably tell you more, the introduction itself has suggestions for how you could adapt a crossover.<br /> <br /> There isn't that much compatibility in this situation, though. The Circle of the Crone worshiped goddesses. These could be spirit gods, they could be just ideas, astral gods, or whatever you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-21-2015, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T08:57:27-07:00","id":487309,"title":"","content":"OK!<br /> <br /> Maybe it would be clearer with examples, it's all still early stages:<br /> <br /> In the game I'm preparing, I want to offer players many options, but for each option, I want them to be embedded into a cohesive tapestry rather than a kitchen sink. Of course, the difference between the two will be my capacity to achieve the desired <i>m\u00e9lange</i>. My challenge is that we are all social science postgraduates who have delved into questions of myth, history, literature, politics, etc. at some point in our lives. We are also geeks, and MST3K mantra applies, but part of the fun is in the suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires</b> (as the primary playable option)<br /> So, it will be a Vampire the Requiem game first and foremost, set in a fictional US East Coast city (and since I'm from Qu\u00e9bec, Canada, the US East Coast is a fun little &quot;exotic&quot; setting to explore), not unlike the Sunnydale, Mystic Falls, Neptune, East End, or Bon Temps of TV Series. (My players are huge fans of these shows, heck I have a player who's doctoral project involves Buffy the Vampire Slayer.) It might very well resemble the fictional city of Newcastle, from Damnation City, or Portland ME, Providence RI, and similar-sized cities.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolves</b> (as the secondary playable option)<br /> Secondarily, but still present, many elements of Werewolf the Forsaken will be integrated. I wand to avoid them being &quot;there&quot; without their spirituality being sufficiently explored, so I need to understand how their history and mythos intersects with Vampires in different historical periods and how that might shape contemporary politics. There will be more than one tribes, and at least one is going to be sympathetic towards the party (for interested reason), and at least one other tribe is going to be outright hostile, though smart about it.<br /> <br /> <b>Covenants</b><br /> To that end, the local Circle of the Crone group is going to be somewhat close to one of the tribes, I'm thinking this would have to be covert. I know my players love Rituals, Blood Magic and the idea of magic having a cost, drawbacks and being somewhat unreliable sometimes.<br /> <br /> I want to Ordo Dracul to be an important covenant, researching ancient secrets and all that. Of course, the other groups might not like all that snooping around, despite the well-mannered members of the order acting so innocuous.<br /> <br /> I intend the Invictus to act as the overarching &quot;Camarilla-style&quot; masquerade enforcer, a greedy powermongering capitalist social club, but an undeniable necessary evil.<br /> <br /> The Carthians will be at odds with the Invictus, but also their extreme-left Anarch rivals. I'm thinking Anarchs in requiem are not very complicated to integrate.<br /> <br /> The Lancea et Sanctum will be aligned with the Religious Conservatives, Evangelical churches and such. Of course, in its own wicked way.<br /> <br /> <b>Clans</b><br /> The Mekhet clan, and its Egyptian background for that matter, needs to be clarified in relation to Mummy the Cursed. I will not integrate playable mummy characters, but I want the mythos to be cross-compatible. Same goes for the origin of &quot;Theban&quot; sorcery, and mentions of goddesses like Isis. I will not do any unadvised name-dropping of Egyptian deities, cities or words without having done my homeworks properly.<br /> <br /> Gangrels will have relations with the local werewolves more than other clans, as well as many members part of the Circle of the Crone.<br /> <br /> Daevas, Ventrue and Nosferatu are going to be mostly where one would expect (meaning: I still have some work to do to think of how to integrate them more, though I don't see them as <i>that</i> complicated).<br /> <br /> Antagonists will likely include the Strix, possessing demons, VII, groups of hunters (including slashers), vampire politics, quite a few werewolves. (And, depending on events, even Judges and Mummies.) That's quite a bit of stuff to tie together, and I want the storyline to have the players guessing who their <i>real </i>enemies are. I'm thinking the role of werewolves as guardians against evil spirits helps a lot to make them want to work with vampires against the greater evil.<br /> <br /> I know I don't intend to use changelings, sin-eaters, geists, wraiths, ghosts, or prometheans much. I might if their metaphysics can integrate seamlessly with the rest. I'm thinking prometheans would be good candidates, if not for their masquerade breaching looks... Changelings, I'd like to integrate, if it doesn't necessitate too many last-minute adjustments and doesn't cause a dirty kitchen sink mess. I just know that for each element I add, my players will have innumerable questions and will expect answers. Of course, not only do I have to find my own hidden answers (or <i>Schr\u00f6dinger's Gun </i>my way through), but I have to craft all the lies in a narratively interesting way for the plot to be multi-faceted enough. Which is why I'm asking all those questions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T09:24:37-07:00","id":487317,"title":"","content":"With Mummy you could have the Mekhet originating from a failed attempt at replicating the ritual that created them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T09:39:06-07:00","id":487348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486069-understanding-the-nwod-current-state-of-mythos-vampires-mummies-rome-egypt-strix?p=487309#post487309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Werewolves</b> (as the secondary playable option)<br /> Secondarily, but still present, many elements of Werewolf the Forsaken will be integrated. I wand to avoid them being &quot;there&quot; without their spirituality being sufficiently explored, so I need to understand how their history and mythos intersects with Vampires in different historical periods and how that might shape contemporary politics. There will be more than one tribes, and at least one is going to be sympathetic towards the party (for interested reason), and at least one other tribe is going to be outright hostile, though smart about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lets start with this.<br /> <br /> First, while vampires and werewolves might bump into each other a lot, they don't have a set perception of one another. Most vampires haven't had the pleasure, and those that do have likely had a wide variety of experiences with werewolves. Unless there was a war of some sort, this likely wouldn't color the perception of an entire court of vampires. If you want there to be a history between the vampires and werewolves in your town, you're going to have to find a reason for there to be one, like the aforementioned war.<br /> <br /> Second, vampire and werewolf mythos is likely to be vastly different. Some werewolves might believe vampires are undead werewolves. Some might believe they're claimed by spirits of hunger and blood. Others might think they're just another kind of supernatural. Werewolves have an entire different level of reality to work off of, that of the Hisil. Werewolves are spiritual hunters that are descendants of Father Wolf and Mother Luna, and patrol the boundaries of the Hisil and the real world. Unless a pack or protectorate or other group has a personal grudge against vampires, they're likely to leave vampires alone until they start earning a hunt. There's currently a Lodge based out of Mongolia that likes to hunt vampires, and the Black Moon eXtreme, though they are pretty bad at it.<br /> <br /> Third, Werewolf the Forsaken tribes aren't like they are in Apocalypse. The core unit of werewolf is the pack, which has members of many tribes and auspices. Outside of a tribe's sacred prey, which they tend to view as a more favorable opponent than others, and the following of the tribal ban, there's not much connecting individual members of the tribes, like there were in Apocalypse. If you wanted to fit into the current World of Darkness, you would want to cut that down to a pack or protectorate that might be sympathetic, and another pack or protectorate that might be hostile. Protectorates are an alliance of packs.<br /> <br /> Fourth, werewolves are divided into four groups. The standard Forsaken, members of the five tribes, they exist to exalt in the sacred hunt and become great hunters, also following the Oath of the Moon and protecting the two worlds from the depredations of their denizens. The Pure, three tribes who hate the Forsaken and have a low view of humanity in general. They exist to tear down the barrier between the worlds and rule, sort of vaguely like the Sabbat. The Ghost Wolves, who are not a member of any tribes and either follow the Oath of the Moon, stick to their own, create cults, or try to form new tribes. And the Bale Hounds, who are serve the Maeljin, demigods of vice and evil.<br /> <br /> Again, there is no metaplot, but knowing a bit more about the individual game lines will help you mix them into your setting without things looking out of place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gangrels and Circle of the Crone </div> </div> </div>If you want these two to be in touch with one another, you're going to have to come up with a reason for it. Werewolves can let vampires into their packs, so why are they letting these guys in? And why is this Circle of the Crone involved with werewolves?<br /> <br /> You might want to keep in mind the political advantage werewolf allies will bring to the table. They are predators that can work in the day and scent out a vampire's haven in moments. If some vampires have them as allies, they're going to have an advantage compared to those that don't.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that the clans are not usually like they were in Masquerade. Members of a clan not by default all working together, and may not even be related.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T09:45:21-07:00","id":487379,"title":"","content":"Oh, also one of the Pure werewolf tribes, the Ivory Claws, <i>really hate</i> vampires. They see all forms of undead as an abomination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T09:57:56-07:00","id":487385,"title":"","content":"They're more likely to avoid them than do anything hostile, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T10:05:45-07:00","id":487389,"title":"","content":"The NWoD has so much vagueness, rumour and possibility because that gives the impression of a grand unifed cosmology which is massively complicated without having to actually come up with one (which isn't really feasible for fiction). If you don't want a kitchen sink, either don't do cross-over, or ditch the idea of a coherent unified cosmology that your players can easily grasp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T10:24:06-07:00","id":487411,"title":"","content":"Also important to understand: the Clans are not super defined by their names, they're reLly just names. There are some among the Mekhet who are technically descended from a group of Kindred called Clan Grettir, that merged over time with the Mekhet and became a part of that Clan. Or maybe they were Mekhet the whole time, by another name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T10:26:53-07:00","id":487422,"title":"","content":"If you want a model for how a city might work with multiple supernatural types, I'd look to the Chicago book for one such example. I think it does a great job of showing how these creatures exist in the same place without necessarily being tied together, which I think is more apropos for the New World of Darkness in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T10:36:50-07:00","id":487429,"title":"","content":"I find that the Big Three + Changeling work together really well if you assume that they really don't bump into each other that often. Running from a Vampire assumption, Werewolves are territorial. When dividing up fiefdoms, the Prince would probably acknowledge certain areas are the domains of wolves, even in the night. Wolves and Vamps are most likely to come into contact, of all the groups, as they both hunt in differing ways. Mages are Big and Scary and basically are way above even top-level Vampire heads. They're the things that keep even the eldest Vampire remembering that they are small and weak and will BURN. They're like, as it where, a giant in the playground, where the politics of vampires probably doesn't really affect them, but they may step on you if you're not watching where one's going. <br /> <br /> Changelings work as the kind of catch-all weird-person type thing. Only a rare vampire knows they exist beyond a run-in with someone who just didn't seem quite right, even with Auspex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T12:37:58-07:00","id":487511,"title":"","content":"Since I'm doing a mixed group, hopefully, with both werewolves and vampires: if the players are interested in forming a &quot;pack&quot;, can vampires invest in the Totem merit and benefit from the perks or is it impossible? I must have read the sidebar in WtF2e, like ten times, the one talking about other supernaturals joining a werewolf pack, saying it's possible, though it's not really clear how functional that is. I thought it might be a neat way to tie both systems together (depending on player choices, of course I would only allow it as part of actual play).<br /> <br /> (And I actually did search on the WtF board for an answer, to no avail.)<br /> <br /> Depending on a lot of factors, simply &quot;maintaining&quot; the pack would already be a challenge, given Kindred politics and other such things. It would require challenges appropriate for both, and a story arc involving otherworldly spirits. I'm thinking maybe a Strix/Demons arc would be interesting to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T12:44:41-07:00","id":487516,"title":"","content":"It's worth considering that each of the different supernatural groups wants something different.<br /> <br /> Vampires need blood, of course, but they're well equipped to get it for themselves under most circumstances. A more precious commodity to them is <i>security</i>. Vampires have perhaps the most restrictive weaknesses of any of the major supernatural types; even mortals stand a decent chance of dispatching an elder vampire if they can find the dark place where he sleeps and figure out how to let a little sunlight in. One of the main reasons that vampires tend to cultivate vast conspiracies and accumulate wealth and power is so that they can prevent just that thing from happening.<br /> <br /> When vampires encounter unfamiliar supernatural beings, they may have any number of reactions, but on some level they're always going to be considering what kind of threat this creature poses to their continued existence. Mages in particular are likely to spook them, particularly if they're not aware that most mages probably can't conjure fireballs from thin air or produce sunlight underground, but the other beings with which they share the night present unique threats as well. Werewolves can track a vampire better than any human, changelings can pop up seemingly anywhere out of some kind of parallel dimension, and so on. Overall, the default reaction is probably for the vampire to avoid being noticed by the other supernatural, though desperate or arrogant bloodsuckers might consider it worth the risk to try and make some kind of deal with them, or to manipulate them toward the vampire's other goals.<br /> <br /> <br /> Forsaken werewolves, on the other hand, are driven less by sheer survival instinct than by what they see as their sacred purpose. No werewolf really expects to die quietly in bed at a ripe old age, and for many werewolves dying is a small price to pay if it helps them accomplish their goals. As such, I can see them taking a more flexible approach to inter-species relations.<br /> <br /> Let's say some crazy Dracula cultist is poisoning a locus with his weird experiments. The local pack will want to put him down, but if they're smart and perceptive, they may realize that he's part of a larger organization that could mean bigger trouble than one lone bloodsucker. They might try to isolate him and take him out without revealing themselves to the other vampires, or they might investigate this vampire society more closely. If they figure out that he has enemies among the other bloodsuckers, they may try to reach some sort of arrangement with them in order to take down the offending leech and perhaps even his entire rotten clique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 04-21-2015, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T12:45:36-07:00","id":487517,"title":"","content":"Yes they can invest in the totem. Rules as written suggest they can only invest one dot, but you can raise that if you want. Everyone in the pack gets the benefit, even if they haven't invested a dot in it. They would also be under the totem's ban. The sidebar says that they can and they're treated like Wolf-blooded, who can only get one dot in the Totem merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T13:08:14-07:00","id":487546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486069-understanding-the-nwod-current-state-of-mythos-vampires-mummies-rome-egypt-strix?p=487517#post487517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes they can invest in the totem. Rules as written suggest they can only invest one dot, but you can raise that if you want. Everyone in the pack gets the benefit, even if they haven't invested a dot in it. They would also be under the totem's ban. The sidebar says that they can and they're treated like Wolf-blooded, who can only get one dot in the Totem merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd just give supernatural pack members the one dot version of the Pack Bond Merit for free and allow them to upgrade to the three dot version for 2 experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T19:06:18-07:00","id":487842,"title":"","content":"After reading a few crossover threads on the VtM/WtA side of things (notably: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/469453-vtm-wta-crossover-suggestions\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...er-suggestions</a>), the whole idea of a &quot;pack&quot; of Vampires and Werewolves was an abhorrent heresy.<br /> <br /> IIRC, in cWoD the Garou fought against the corruption of the Wyrm, of which both &quot;evil corporations&quot; and vampires were considered a part of. Are there mythological / spiritual reasons why the Uratha wouldn't want to associate with vampires, apart from the fact each group &quot;wants something different&quot;? Are vampires universally considered an &quot;affront to nature&quot; by the Forsaken, or is it more complicated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T19:25:53-07:00","id":487855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486069-understanding-the-nwod-current-state-of-mythos-vampires-mummies-rome-egypt-strix?p=487842#post487842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading a few crossover threads on the VtM/WtA side of things (notably: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/469453-vtm-wta-crossover-suggestions\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...er-suggestions</a>), the whole idea of a &quot;pack&quot; of Vampires and Werewolves was an abhorrent heresy.<br /> <br /> IIRC, in cWoD the Garou fought against the corruption of the Wyrm, of which both &quot;evil corporations&quot; and vampires were considered a part of. Are there mythological / spiritual reasons why the Uratha wouldn't want to associate with vampires, apart from the fact each group &quot;wants something different&quot;? Are vampires universally considered an &quot;affront to nature&quot; by the Forsaken, or is it more complicated?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, no such inherent animosity between them in nWoD.<br /> <br /> Now, to be fair, the presence of a large vampire population <i>can</i> have pretty potent impact on the local spirit world. They'd be a plentiful source of death-resonant essence, among other things. Different Uratha will have different reactions to this, as with any unusual spirit activity. Some packs may be very upset about the local vampires messing up their territory's spiritual balance, while others might be indifferent or even find it to be a positive influence. It's all down to the individual, there is no one way that all werewolves feel about all vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T19:31:03-07:00","id":487858,"title":"","content":"VtM and WtA are vastly different games from VtR and WtF.<br /> <br /> Werewolves and vampires don't have universal beliefs on anything, except obvious things like hunting and blood is good, or silver and sunlight is bad. Some vampires believe they're cursed by god, some believe they're gifted by the Crone, some think it's just a disease, and the strix say they started it all.<br /> <br /> As I said, some werewolves might think vampires are the souls of dead werewolves, or spirit-claimed. And if vampires are particularly chaotic, they can bring out spirits that the werewolves might not like on their territory. What spirits werewolves won't like on their territory is going to depend on the individual pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T20:03:14-07:00","id":487903,"title":"","content":"You can look into Dark Eras or the historical settings for Requiem 1.0 about Rome or Ancient Mysteries. It is more history happened more or less as we know it and this is how vampires interacted within that history. The first rule of history as a vampire is if you didn't witness it then you don't know what happened any more than anyone else. Vampires don't need a fog because they lie. The winners write the history books, as they say. History is really &quot;history&quot; except in a broad general sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T22:23:39-07:00","id":487986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BarbeChenue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486069-understanding-the-nwod-current-state-of-mythos-vampires-mummies-rome-egypt-strix?p=487842#post487842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading a few crossover threads on the VtM/WtA side of things (notably: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/469453-vtm-wta-crossover-suggestions\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...er-suggestions</a>), the whole idea of a &quot;pack&quot; of Vampires and Werewolves was an abhorrent heresy.<br /> <br /> IIRC, in cWoD the Garou fought against the corruption of the Wyrm, of which both &quot;evil corporations&quot; and vampires were considered a part of. Are there mythological / spiritual reasons why the Uratha wouldn't want to associate with vampires, apart from the fact each group &quot;wants something different&quot;? Are vampires universally considered an &quot;affront to nature&quot; by the Forsaken, or is it more complicated?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll echo the fact that they aren't; in fact, Iron Masters probably respect them, precisely for the reason they respect all humans and human variants; they're dangerous and clever enough to qualify as worthy prey (Iron Masters have a wonderful love/hate relationship with humans-they honestly do think humans are the most dangerous to the balance between spirit and flesh, but this isn't a slight against humanity, it's just a sign of how powerful sapience is as a concept).<br /> <br /> In fact, I'd say many more religious Uratha and the Sanctified would get along like a house on fire; the Lanacea et Sanctum wants to protect their flock as well as instill the fear of God into it, and werewolves think of themselves as protectors of humans from a vicious spirit world. If it became clear the spirits were a threat to the Sanctified's human charges, well, you take what you're given, and in the case of a race of hyperpowerful trackers and warriors, the Lord is generous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T04:03:07-07:00","id":488121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486069-understanding-the-nwod-current-state-of-mythos-vampires-mummies-rome-egypt-strix?p=486475#post486475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a Mummy guy, I can confirm that it's pretty explicit about the origins of its protagonists: all Mummies were created by the sorcerer-priests of the Nameless Empire during the Rite of Return 6000 years ago. They were selected from the ranks of middle-class laborers, guildsmen, crafters, priests, and lawyers. The guilds were formed by the sorcerer-kings to be specialized labor, naturally.<br /> <br /> There <i>are</i> lots of questions that arise in the setting, but few of them are related to history or origins. They're more like, &quot;What was I doing between 456 and 500 CE, and why does it seem to have something to do with the ancient ghosts of these Roman Legionnaires and a seedy corporate cult trying to steal my relics?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the Cheiron Group?! Because that's the vibe i'm getting, though they might be more greek than roman... :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486069-understanding-the-nwod-current-state-of-mythos-vampires-mummies-rome-egypt-strix?p=486573#post486573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but ponder how Father Wolf being a Lunar <i>would</i> explain a few things, like how werewolves ended up half-human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, many funny ways things could work out or mix indeed - connecting the dots in ways that tell old stories in novel forms is half the fun.<br /> <br /> OP, on the matter of fodder for mixed groups Chicago can be useful as others have mentioned, but one i would seriously reccomend looking into is Shadows over Mexico, for the great work they do in playing around with customization and the potential of regional variation in the myths and institutions of supernaturals due to local culture &amp; history, both mundane and secret. Damn, there are clan descriptions and origin myths from a pre-columbian perspective and mention one prince with werewolves as a group making part of his court, just for a few examples. Check it out, it will be really worth your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T05:50:52-07:00","id":488185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486069-understanding-the-nwod-current-state-of-mythos-vampires-mummies-rome-egypt-strix?p=488121#post488121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, the Cheiron Group?! Because that's the vibe i'm getting, though they might be more greek than roman... :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy has its own corporate antagonist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T18:16:11-07:00","id":488903,"title":"","content":"Hmm... now that I think about it, I'd love to see the World of Darkness version of <a href=\"http://www.theyrule.net/\" target=\"_blank\">theyrule.net</a>. I wouldn't be surprised if some of the same people (or <i>things</i>) sit on the boards of <i>both </i>evil corporate conspiracies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T11:52:33-07:00","id":499192,"title":"","content":"Is there anything in the pipeline to reconcile rank in the Ordo Dracul with the changes Blood &amp; Smoke/2nd Edition made to the Coils of the Dragon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T11:56:55-07:00","id":499198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/486069-understanding-the-nwod-current-state-of-mythos-vampires-mummies-rome-egypt-strix?p=499192#post499192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything in the pipeline to reconcile rank in the Ordo Dracul with the changes Blood &amp; Smoke/2nd Edition made to the Coils of the Dragon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it still works. More Coils = higher rank, where's the problem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T13:51:57-07:00","id":499360,"title":"","content":"I think the issue would be ranks based on 3 dot coils that now have 5 dots so before at the highest rank you would have mastered 3 coils if you stuck to the 3 main ones while 9 dots of coils now means you might not have mastered any. Out of the box, the maximum dots jumped from 9 to 15 and the ranks only went up to 9.<br /> <br /> It might be addressed in the upcoming Secrets of the Covenants. Until then, Blood is Voivode, Beast is Wyrm, Banes is Ascendant. I guess you can stick with the ranks as they are written until someone changes it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 05-01-2015, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T14:00:52-07:00","id":499369,"title":"","content":"Or just up the number of dots required to attain a given rank. 1-2, 3-4, 5, rather than each individual dot. They're a <i>little</i> easier to objectively codify in some cases. New titles pertaining to scales would be cool too. Hmm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T15:58:27-07:00","id":499463,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't be surprised if that kind of stuff is in SotC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T16:07:25-07:00","id":499471,"title":"","content":"Here's hoping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T23:21:15-07:00","id":499888,"title":"","content":"I would wait to spread out the ranks until you get to Adept. It would be easy to just start numbering First, Second, etc. for each rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}